[Themes "same-setup,attack-d4"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. d4 d5 2. Nf3 ( 2. g3 Nf6 3. Bg2 e6 4. Nf3 Be7 )
( 2. c3 Nf6 3. Nf3 e6 4. Bg5 h6 { Asks the bishop what it wants. } 5. Bxf6 Qxf6 6. Nbd2 c5 )
2... Nf6 3. g3 e6 { Black builds the same set-up: ...Nf6, ...e6, ...Be7, castle, ...c5, ...Nc6. A bishop on g2 changes little, but the diagonal pressure on d5 means Black must keep the centre solid. }
4. Bg2 Be7 { Covers f6 and d6 and gets ready to castle. } 5. O-O O-O { Safe king first, then the central break. } 6. Nbd2 c5 { Strikes at d4 and takes the centre fight to White's side. }
7. c3 Nc6 { Another attacker on d4. White cannot keep both the centre and the pawn on d4 easily. } 8. dxc5 Bxc5 { Plan: ...b6 and ...Bb7, or ...e5 to take the centre. White's bishop on g2 will not do much if Black keeps d5 protected. } *
